  "result": "Perfect! All 97 tests pass. I've successfully implemented VAT (Value Added Tax) support:\n\n**Key implementations:**\n\n1. **lineVat(line)** function\n   - Calculates VAT on the line's amount after discount: (lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate \u00f7 100\n   - Rounded to whole cents per line\n\n2. **Updated invoiceTotals()** to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n   - `vat` = sum of rounded per-line VATs (not a percentage of invoice total)\n   - `total` = subtotal \u2212 discount + vat, clamped at 0\n\n3. **Updated renderInvoiceText()**\n   - Shows \"VAT: \u20acamount\" line just above the total (only if VAT > 0)\n   - Displays all amounts formatted through formatEuros()\n\n4. **Comprehensive tests covering:**\n   - VAT at different rates (0%, 9%, 21% per catalogue)\n   - VAT on discounted amounts\n   - Multiple lines with mixed VAT rates\n   - Proper per-line rounding and summation\n   - Total clamping at zero with VAT\n   - Integration with discounts and tier discounts\n\n**Example calculation:**\n- Product: \u20ac1,200 (120,000 cents) at 21% VAT\n- With 5% discount: \u20ac60 discount, taxable \u20ac1,140\n- VAT: \u20ac1,140 \u00d7 21% = \u20ac239.40\n- Total: \u20ac1,200 \u2212 \u20ac60 + \u20ac239.40 = \u20ac1,379.40",
